From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: a home screen with this device's applications on it

The home screen came up with nothing on it. AOSP fills it from
default_workspace_5x6.xml, which places a hotseat of Google applications, the
contacts application and the market; this device has none of those, so every
entry was dropped. The browser was then placed by the launcher itself,
wherever it found room, which is not where someone would put it ("目前首页只有
浏览器，且位置不在屏幕第一格", user, 2026-10-19).

The layout now names what this device has, starting with WeRead: before it is
installed the cell holds the installer's own entry, which says so and offers
to fetch it, because nothing else on the device ever mentions that WeRead can
be had here ("用户完全感知不到", same day). Row 0 of the first screen is the
search box (0004), so the applications start at row 1.

diff --git a/res/xml/default_workspace_5x6.xml b/res/xml/default_workspace_5x6.xml
index 8493c26..0b2f321 100644
--- a/res/xml/default_workspace_5x6.xml
+++ b/res/xml/default_workspace_5x6.xml
@@ -14,24 +14,50 @@
      limitations under the License.
 -->
 
+<!-- PW3: what is on the home screen the first time it is opened. AOSP put a
+     hotseat of Google applications here, with contacts and the market below
+     them; this device has none of those, so every entry was dropped and the
+     home screen came up empty. The first application installed then landed
+     wherever the launcher found room, which is the row under the search box
+     and not where someone would put it.
+
+     Row 0 of the first screen is the search box (0004), so the applications
+     start at row 1, in the order they are reached for: read, then the web,
+     then what is stored, then settings.
+
+     The first of them is WeRead before WeRead is installed: the installer own
+     entry (WeReadInstaller/StatusActivity), under WeRead name and an icon
+     that says it is a download. Without it nothing on this device says that
+     WeRead can be had here at all. It takes itself off once WeRead is
+     installed, and WeRead own icon is placed in the cell it leaves. -->
 <favorites xmlns:launcher="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto/com.android.launcher3">
 
-    <!-- Hotseat -->
-    <include launcher:workspace="@xml/dw_tablet_hotseat" />
-
-    <!-- Bottom row -->
     <favorite
         launcher:screen="0"
         launcher:x="0"
-        launcher:y="-1"
-        launcher:uri="#Intent;action=android.intent.action.MAIN;category=android.intent.category.APP_CONTACTS;end" />
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="org.readom.wereadinstaller"
+        launcher:className="org.readom.wereadinstaller.StatusActivity" />
+
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="1"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="info.plateaukao.einkbro"
+        launcher:className="info.plateaukao.einkbro.activity.BrowserActivity" />
 
-    <resolve
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="2"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="com.android.documentsui"
+        launcher:className="com.android.documentsui.LauncherActivity" />
+
+    <favorite
         launcher:screen="0"
-        launcher:x="-1"
-        launcher:y="-1" >
-        <favorite launcher:uri="#Intent;action=android.intent.action.MAIN;category=android.intent.category.APP_MARKET;end" />
-        <favorite launcher:uri="market://details?id=com.android.launcher" />
-    </resolve>
+        launcher:x="3"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="com.android.settings"
+        launcher:className="com.android.settings.Settings" />
 
 </favorites>
